// SR 810.12 — Chapter 8 Criminal Provisions
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 56 Misdemeanours
1 A person shall be liable to a custodial sentence not exceeding three years or to a monetary penalty if he or she wilfully:
a. prescribes, arranges or performs a genetic test or creates or arranges a DNA profile without obtaining the consent of the person being tested required under this Act;
b. in the course of his or her professional activity, discloses information on a person’s genetic material to that person against that person’s will;
c. prescribes or arranges a genetic test on a person incapable of judgement that is neither required for the protection of that person’s health nor meets the requirements of Article 16 paragraph 2;
|

:INFO
Art. 56 (continued)
d. prescribes or arranges prenatal genetic tests that neither serve to clarify characteristics that directly impair the health of the embryo or foetus, nor to clarify blood groups or blood characteristics in accordance with Article 17 paragraph 1 letter b, nor to clarify tissue characteristics in accordance with Article 17 paragraph 1 letter c;
e. in connection with employment or insurance, requires non-medical genetic tests to be performed, asks for medically irrelevant genetic data or makes use of such data;
f. contrary to Article 39 letter a, requires or prescribes presymptomatic genetic tests in connection with employment, without meeting the requirements of Article 40;
g. contrary to Article 39 letter b, requires or makes use of the results of prior presymptomatic genetic tests in connection with employment;
h. contrary to Article 42, requires presymptomatic or prenatal genetic tests or tests for family planning in connection with insurance;
|

:INFO
Art. 56 (continued)
i. contrary to Article 43, requires genetic data from prior presymptomatic or prenatal genetic tests or tests for family planning or makes use of such data in connection with insurance;
2 A person shall be liable to a custodial sentence not exceeding three years or to a monetary penalty if he or she wilfully and in the course of a professional activity:
a. fails to destroy samples or genetic data from tests in accordance with Article 31 paragraph 2 within two years where the person concerned has not given express consent for their use for another purpose (Art. 11 para. 2);
b. contrary to Articles 12 or 44 paragraph 3, uses samples or genetic data for another purpose;
c. contrary to Article 13 supplies persons concerned with genetic tests for self-testing in a medical context, to clarify sensitive non-medical personality characteristics or to create DNA profiles to establish filiation or a person’s identity;
|

:INFO
Art. 56 (continued)
d. prescribes a genetic test in a medical context without fulfilling the requirements of Article 20;
e. prescribes a genetic test to clarify sensitive characteristics without being entitled to do so in accordance with Article 34 paragraphs 1, 2 and 4.
|

:INFO
Art. 57 Contraventions
A person is liable to a fine if he or she wilfully:
a. infringes the ban on advertising to the public under Article 14 paragraph 1 or advertises products or services to the public in which the information on the provisions of the Act required by Article 14 paragraph 3 or Article 47 paragraph 4 is false or missing;
b. discloses to a pregnant woman before the end of the twelfth week of pregnancy the gender of the embryo or foetus contrary to Article 17 paragraph 2 letter a or Article 52 paragraph 3 or the results of the test for tissue characteristics contrary to Article 17 paragraph 2 letter b;
c. performs a genetic test on a third party’s genetic material without possessing the required authorisation;
d. performs DNA profiling on a third party without possessing the required recognition.
|

:INFO
Art. 58 Competent authority and administrative criminal law
1 The cantons shall be responsible for the prosecution and adjudication of offences under this Act.
2 Articles 6 and 7 on offences committed within a company and Article 15 on forgery, and on obtaining a false certificate by fraud of the Federal Act of 22 March 1974 on Administrative Criminal Law apply.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — SR 313.0

